# XSH posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Effects are shown by really spawning this program as a child image (the
# test file re-runs itself with "img <mode>" arguments and reports over a
# pipe). The function returns the error number; errno is not used.

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.001
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2() with an open descriptor and a
           different number returns 0.
test       t/001-ok.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.002
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawn.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       A child spawned with a dup2 action from fildes (a file read to offset 3)
           to newfildes (not open in the parent) can read at newfildes
           the bytes that follow in the file, and the parent's offset on
           fildes then reflects that read (one open file description).
test       t/002-effect.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.003
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawn.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       When fildes has FD_CLOEXEC set and newfildes differs, the child has
           newfildes open with FD_CLOEXEC clear (it was made by dup2)
           and fildes closed.
test       t/003-cloexec-source.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.004
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.html#RATIONALE
class      required
since      2024
says       When fildes and newfildes are the same open descriptor with FD_CLOEXEC
           set, the child has it open (same file) with FD_CLOEXEC clear.
test       t/004-equal-clears.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.005
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       When newfildes is already open in the parent (on another file), the
           child's newfildes refers to the file of fildes.
test       t/005-replaces.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.006
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2() with a negative fildes, and with a
           negative newfildes (each -1 and the most negative int),
           returns EBADF.
test       t/006-ebadf-neg.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.007
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2() with fildes equal to {OPEN_MAX}, and
           with newfildes equal to {OPEN_MAX}, returns EBADF.
note       See Q-90 (the RATIONALE of addclose against the shall of adddup2).
test       t/007-ebadf-max.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.008
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.html#ERRORS
anchor     functions/posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawn.html#ERRORS
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2() with a source number that is not open
           at the time of the call returns 0; a spawn with that action
           does not run the image: posix_spawn() returns an error
           number, or the child exits with status 127.
test       t/008-notopen.c
